From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wzc-claude <wzc-claude@local>
Date: Tue, 22 Sep 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] MUSA: page-align KV-first blocks in the packed KV slab

In the packed layout every cache group lays its pages over the same block
slab, so correctness rests on a block ID being owned by one group at a time.
A KV-first cache shape such as (2, num_blocks, ...) broke that: the view
strided the kv dimension by one whole slab block and the block dimension by
one page, so block b covered neither page b nor a page of its own group, and
its writes landed in the pages other groups held in different slab blocks.

Build the view page-first for those shapes and swap the dimensions back, so
block b covers page b again. Block-first shapes are unchanged.

---
--- a/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/attn_utils.py
+++ b/vllm/v1/worker/gpu/attn_utils.py
@@ -298,14 +298,35 @@
         packed_kv_cache = kv_raw_tensor.view(-1, block_stride)[
             :, offset : offset + page_bytes
         ].view(dtype)
-        inner_shape = permuted_kv_cache_shape[1:]
+        if permuted_kv_cache_shape[0] == num_blocks:
+            page_shape = permuted_kv_cache_shape
+            kv_first = False
+        else:
+            # A KV-first layout such as ``(2, num_blocks, ...)`` would stride
+            # the block dimension by one page and the kv dimension by one whole
+            # slab block, so block ``b`` would not cover page ``b`` and would
+            # resolve the bytes another cache group holds in a different slab
+            # block. Build the view page-first and swap the dims back.
+            assert permuted_kv_cache_shape[1] == num_blocks, (
+                "Packed KV pages need the block dimension first or second (got "
+                f"shape {permuted_kv_cache_shape} with num_blocks={num_blocks})."
+            )
+            page_shape = (
+                num_blocks,
+                permuted_kv_cache_shape[0],
+                *permuted_kv_cache_shape[2:],
+            )
+            kv_first = True
+        inner_shape = page_shape[1:]
         inner_strides = [1] * len(inner_shape)
         for i in range(len(inner_shape) - 2, -1, -1):
             inner_strides[i] = inner_strides[i + 1] * inner_shape[i + 1]
         kv_cache = packed_kv_cache.as_strided(
-            permuted_kv_cache_shape,
+            page_shape,
             (packed_kv_cache.stride(0), *inner_strides),
         )
+        if kv_first:
+            kv_cache = kv_cache.transpose(0, 1)
     elif kv_cache_spec.page_size_padded is not None:
         # Use a strided view to skip the padding between physical pages.
         #
